    [Feature][PCP][v0.30.0] Support graph execution for sharded decode requests (#18196)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Backport #17958 to `releases/v0.30.0` for the dual merge. The
    prerequisite #17456 is already included in the release branch.
    
    Enable PCP decode request sharding under PIECEWISE and FULL
    (FULL_DECODE_ONLY) graph execution. Align rank-local graph dispatch,
    padded metadata and empty-rank handling, and keep DSA global RoPE
    buffers at graph-stable addresses. Preserve the upstream dispatch
    workaround documented by the original PR.
    
    Cherry-picked source commit: `44358abf686dc64ef3effec70d800a89a03662b6`,
    with original authorship, sign-offs and source reference preserved. No
    conflict resolution or additional changes were required.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. Eligible non-speculative PCP configurations shard decode requests
    under graph execution instead of using the replicated decode path.
    Speculative decoding retains the replicated path, as in #17958.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - The stable patch ID matches merged #17958 exactly
    (`fec459eb8d81f9fbc3e84c2c2e1d5c2ab15df9fe`).
    - `git diff --check upstream/releases/v0.30.0...HEAD` passed.
    - Includes the original regression updates in
    `tests/ut/worker/test_model_runner_v2.py`,
    `tests/ut/worker/test_pcp_manager_v2.py` and
    `tests/ut/attention/test_dsa_v1.py`.
    - Attempted `bash format.sh ci` using Git Bash; it could not run because
    pre-commit is not installed in the local environment. Full lint and
    release-branch regression verification remain for CI.
    - No new NPU runtime, accuracy or performance validation was performed
    for this backport.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/ced6857afa0ea7b2e3f0846a62e1394e90f15607
    
    Signed-off-by: recky-c <ruiqicheng510@gmail.com>
    Signed-off-by: chengruiqi (C) <c00913489@china.huawei.com>
